
<section id=" faq ">
  <div class=" wrap faq-grid ">
    <div class=" faq-left ">
      <div class=" eyebrow ">Common Questions</div>
      <h2 class=" display " style=" margin-top:14px ">What people ask before buying</h2>
      <p class=" sub ">If something isn't answered here, our team responds within one business day.</p>
      <a class=" contact " href=" mailto:hello@reviveteeth.com ">Contact us → </a>
    </div>
    <div class=" faq-list " id=" faqList ">
      <div class=" faq-item ">
        <button class=" faq-q ">
          Should I get both arches or single arch?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div class=" faq-a ">
          <div>
            <p>
              Most buyers choose both arches because upper-only veneers can look unnatural when you smile or talk. The
              bottom teeth show in roughly 80% of smile photos, and a color mismatch between veneered upper teeth and
              natural lower teeth is the most common reason people stop wearing snap-on veneers. We recommend both
              arches unless your lower teeth are already in good shape. At $1,997 for both vs. $1,497 for single, the
              upgrade pays for itself in long-term satisfaction.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          Am I a candidate for Revive Veneers?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              Most people are. Revive Veneers work well for anyone with healthy teeth and gums who wants to improve the
              appearance of stained, slightly gapped, or worn teeth. They aren't right for people with active gum
              disease, severe bite issues, multiple missing teeth at the end of the arch, or anyone currently wearing
              full dentures. We recommend taking our 30-second Smile Assessment before ordering if you're unsure.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          What happens after I order?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              Your impression kit ships within 48 hours. You take impressions at home (about 5 minutes), mail them back
              free, and your custom veneers arrive 2–3 weeks after we receive them. Dr. Turley designs every case in
              between.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          Can I cancel after ordering?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              Yes, before your impressions arrive at the lab. Once we receive your impressions and Dr. Turley begins the
              smile design, the order can't be cancelled because each veneer is custom-designed for your mouth. If your
              veneers don't fit comfortably, we remake them at no cost. If we still can't get it right, you receive a
              full refund within 30 days of delivery.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          Can I split the payment into installments?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              We don't offer in-page financing or third-party lenders. If you'd like to split your payment into 3
              installments, email us at
              <a
                href=" mailto:hello@reviveteeth.com?subject=Revive%20Veneers%20%E2%80%94%20Split%20payment%20request "
                >hello@reviveteeth.com
              </a>
              and we'll arrange it directly. No interest, no fees, no third parties.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          What if I'm missing teeth?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              Snap-on veneers can cover gaps and improve the appearance of one or two missing front teeth, provided the
              missing teeth are not at the end of the arch. We need teeth at the back of your arch for the veneer to
              anchor to. If you have multiple missing teeth, or teeth missing at the end of the arch, or you wear full
              dentures, snap-on veneers aren't the right solution. Take our Smile Assessment to find out, or send photos
              to Dr. Turley for review before ordering.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          Will my impressions be good enough?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              The kit includes two batches of dental putty so you can take impressions twice if needed. The instructions
              are clear and the process takes about 5 minutes. If your impressions don't capture enough detail when we
              receive them, we send you a second kit free of charge.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          How long do the veneers last?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              3 to 5+ years with proper care. The veneers are made from durable dental-grade resin and stored in a
              protective case when not worn. To maximize lifespan: clean daily with a soft toothbrush, remove for hard
              or sticky foods, and avoid using your teeth as tools.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          Can I eat with them in?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              Yes for most foods. We recommend removing them for hard foods (apples, nuts, raw vegetables) and sticky
              foods (caramel, taffy) to extend their lifespan. Soft and chewy foods are fine.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          Will they stain?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              Revive Veneers are made from stain-resistant dental resin, but they can discolor over time with heavy
              coffee, tea, red wine, or tobacco exposure. Daily cleaning prevents most staining.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class=" faq-item "
      >
        <button
          class=" faq-q "
        >
          Where do you ship?
          <svg
            class=" chev "
            viewBox=" 0 0 24 24 "
            fill=" none "
            stroke=" currentColor "
            stroke-width=" 2 "
          >
            <path
                d=" M6 9l6 6 6-6 ">
                </path>
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div
          class=" faq-a "
        >
          <div>
            <p>
              US only at this time. Shipping is free both ways within the continental US, including Alaska and Hawaii.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% schema %}
  {
    "name": "Faq",
    "settings": []
  }
  {% endschema %}